# ---------------------------------------------------------------- source data
# CHB-MIT is 45.76 GB of clinical paediatric EEG under ODC-BY, redistributed by
# PhysioNet. It is never committed: too large, and not ours to mirror. The
# pipeline downloads and verifies it (`make ingest`), so a clone reproduces it
# from the authoritative source rather than from a stale copy.
seizure-detection/data/
EEG_Scaled_data.csv
*.edf
*.edf.seizures

# --------------------------------------------------------- derived bulk output
# 697 MB of feature parquet, regenerated by the ingest/extract pipeline. The
# extraction_hash in configs/base.yaml pins exactly what these should contain,
# so committing them would add weight without adding trust.
seizure-detection/artifacts/features/
seizure-detection/artifacts/csv_scaled_features.parquet
seizure-detection/artifacts/runs/

# The fitted estimator IS committed, as a deliberate exception. At compress=3
# the forest is 8.5 MB rather than 29.7 MB and loads in half a second, which is
# small enough that the hosted demo needs no separate model-hosting step and a
# clone can run the upload tab immediately. Rebuild it with:
#   seizure fit-final --view aggregated --loso-detail artifacts/rfjoint_base/detail_aggregated.json
# Any other pickled model stays out.
*.joblib
!seizure-detection/artifacts/final_model_aggregated.joblib

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- reports
# The small result files ARE committed on purpose -- report.md/json, the
# detail_*.json runs and the frozen snapshots under artifacts/. They are the
# project's findings, they are what the app and README cite, and they are the
# only way a reader can check a quoted number without a 45 GB download.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- toolchain
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ scratch/OS
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
